{
  "workflow_id": "pack-agent-trade-evidence",
  "name": "Agent Trade Evidence",
  "outcome": "A nine-stage agent trade evidence workflow over caller-declared inputs. Step 1 validates the trading agent's on-behalf-of mandate, its subject, scope, intent and validity window, and step 2 then applies a fixed ten-rule authorization order to the declared mandate, budget, rail state and proposed request. Step 3 aggregates the declared oracle submissions into the single price an oracle network would publish, and step 4 then publishes the head event that sequence-numbers the mark-price print stream. Step 5 slices the declared order into VWAP, TWAP and participation-of-volume schedules and decomposes implementation shortfall; step 6 then scores every declared fill for price improvement against the NBBO at execution, and step 7 weighs the declared per-venue figures into a monitoring evidence pack with an overall verdict. Step 8 validates the agent's audit-trail records for completeness and chain-link conformance, and step 9 then aggregates the session into one Merkle-root receipt with inclusion proofs. Each step computes from its own declared inputs; the order is analytical, not a statutory sequence, and the chain certifies nothing.",
